: [01:46:32 -> 01:46:36] and sexual confusion and out of jail and all these things.\r\n19: [01:46:36 -> 01:46:41] And I was listening to them.\r\n20: [01:46:41 -> 01:46:45] I was thinking to myself, what is it that I really want to impart\r\n21: [01:46:45 -> 01:46:46] to others?\r\n22: [01:46:46 -> 01:46:49] What is it that I want to impart to people?\r\n23: [01:46:49 -> 01:46:50] We're facing all these things.\r\n24: [01:46:50 -> 01:46:52] What do I really want to transfer of what I have\r\n25: [01:46:52 -> 01:46:55] and what I've laid a hold of in my life?\r\n26: [01:46:55 -> 01:46:58] And I thought, do I have advice for every situation\r\n27: [01:46:58 -> 01:46:58] that they face?\r\n28: [01:46:58 -> 01:47:00] Maybe I've faced a little of what they face,\r\n29: [01:47:00 -> 01:47:05] but nowhere near the same circumstances and trials.\r\n30: [01:47:05 -> 01:47:08] So I don't really have advice that I can give.\r\n31: [01:47:08 -> 01:47:11] And I was thinking, is it just more biblical how-tos?\r\n32: [01:47:11 -> 01:47:14] Do I just want to say, here's the way that you do this\r\n33: [01:47:14 -> 01:47:17] and you do this?\r\n34: [01:47:17 -> 01:47:18] And I was just really thinking to myself,\r\n35: [01:47:18 -> 01:47:22] like what is the good news that I want to communicate to people?\r\n36: [01:47:22 -> 01:47:27] And I was thinking of first Peter, chapter 3,\r\n37: [01:47:27 -> 01:47:30] talks about being ready.\r\n38: [01:47:30 -> 01:47:32] He's talking about the when we're slandered\r\n39: [01:47:32 -> 01:47:35] and we're maligned by people.\r\n40: [01:47:35 -> 01:47:44] But that verse in first Peter, 3.15, he says,\r\n41: [01:47:44 -> 01:47:47] to always be ready to make a defense to everyone who asks you\r\n42: [01:47:47 -> 01:47:52] to give an account for the hope that is in you.\r\n43: [01:47:52 -> 01:47:54] And that word defense, actually, that's\r\n44: [01:47:54 -> 01:47:56] where we get our modern word for apologetics.\r\n45: [01:47:56 -> 01:47:58] And when you think about apologetics most of the time,\r\n46: [01:47:58 -> 01:48:01] it's just knowledge.\r\n47: [01:48:01 -> 01:48:02] Let me defend creation.\r\n48: [01:48:02 -> 01:48:04] And let me defend the historicity\r\n49: [01:48:04 -> 01:48:10] of the Bible in Jesus or moral philosophy arguments.\r\n50: [01:48:10 -> 01:48:11] And there's a place for that.\r\n51: [01:48:11 -> 01:48:15] But what Peter must have been talking about here,\r\n52: [01:48:15 -> 01:48:17] he starts first Peter, 3.15, he says,\r\n53: [01:48:17 -> 01:48:20] but sanctify Christ as Lord in your hearts.\r\n54: [01:48:20 -> 01:48:24] There's no sanctifying Lord as Christ as Lord in your hearts.\r\n55: [01:48:24 -> 01:48:27] That's necessary to fill your head with knowledge and arguments.\r\n56: [01:48:27 -> 01:48:32] But the hope that Paul wants us to give an answer for,\r\n57: [01:48:32 -> 01:48:36] that hope requires that Jesus is first in our hearts.\r\n58: [01:48:36 -> 01:48:38] And he's the Lord of our hearts.\r\n59: [01:48:38 -> 01:48:44] And I was thinking of that verse in Colossians,\r\n60: [01:48:44 -> 01:48:45] a few verses in Colossians chapter one that\r\n61: [01:48:45 -> 01:48:48] expressed this hope that we have as believers\r\n62: [01:48:48 -> 01:48:53] and that I want to be the anthem of my life.\r\n63: [01:48:53 -> 01:49:01] Colossians 1 verse 25 of this church I was made a minister.\r\n64: [01:49:01 -> 01:49:04] And he says, at the end of verse 25, Colossians 1.25,\r\n65: [01:49:04 -> 01:49:07] so that I might fully carry out the preaching of the word of God.\r\n66: [01:49:07 -> 01:49:08] Here's the gospel.\r\n67: [01:49:08 -> 01:49:11] That is, the mystery which has been hidden from past ages\r\n68: [01:49:11 -> 01:49:18] and generations, but has now been manifested to his saints,\r\n69: [01:49:18 -> 01:49:20] to whom God will to make known what is the riches\r\n70: [01:49:20 -> 01:49:23] of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles,\r\n71: [01:49:23 -> 01:49:27] which is Christ in you, the hope of glory.\r\n72: [01:49:28 -> 01:49:30] And so the hope that I want to share,\r\n73: [01:49:30 -> 01:49:32] what I want to impart, if I could have an anthem for my life,\r\n74: [01:49:32 -> 01:49:34] if I could have something that I could give to every person,\r\n75: [01:49:34 -> 01:49:36] every lost person that I come across,\r\n76: [01:49:36 -> 01:49:39] every person, another believer,\r\n77: [01:49:39 -> 01:49:42] wherever they are in maturity, it's this life\r\n78: [01:49:42 -> 01:49:43] that Christ is dwelling in me.\r\n79: [01:49:43 -> 01:49:45] Christ is producing his glory in me.\r\n80: [01:49:45 -> 01:49:47] Christ is forming something in me.\r\n81: [01:49:47 -> 01:49:48] It's more than right answers.\r\n82: [01:49:48 -> 01:49:52] It's that Christ has set apart his Lord and my heart\r\n83: [01:49:52 -> 01:49:57] and he's the life and the theme of my existence,\r\n84: [01:49:59 -> 01:50:00] my being.\r\n85: [01:50:00 -> 01:50:02] I was thinking about if you've ever had\r\n86: [01:50:03 -> 01:50:06] or made kombucha or kafir or sourdough,\r\n87: [01:50:08 -> 01:50:10] all these different things that have this,\r\n88: [01:50:10 -> 01:50:13] they have like a living and an active culture.\r\n89: [01:50:13 -> 01:50:16] And then I could give somebody a cup.\r\n90: [01:50:16 -> 01:50:17] It's like, I give you, here's the advice.\r\n91: [01:50:17 -> 01:50:18] I've faced this situation.\r\n92: [01:50:18 -> 01:50:19] Maybe I haven't faced this one.\r\n93: [01:50:19 -> 01:50:20] I don't have advice on that one.\r\n94: [01:50:20 -> 01:50:23] I give you a cup here because I've made this cup of kombucha\r\n95: [01:50:23 -> 01:50:26] and you try, like, all kombucha is pretty good.\r\n96: [01:50:28 -> 01:50:30] But how much better would it be\r\n97: [01:50:33 -> 01:50:35] if I could give somebody the life?\r\n98: [01:50:35 -> 01:50:37] Like, if you give somebody, if I say,\r\n99: [01:50:37 -> 01:50:38] here's I think they call it a mother with kombucha\r\n100: [01:50:38 -> 01:50:43] or kafir, it's the grain or there's something alive.\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
